    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNestled within a mature and well-established residential neighbourhood, 91 Pearse Gardens is an attractive two-bedroom home extending to approximately 69 sq.m. (743 sq.ft.), offering bright, well-proportioned accommodation complemented by excellent outdoor space and exceptional parking facilities. Ideal for first-time buyers, downsizers or investors alike, this charming property combines comfort, convenience and practicality in a highly desirable location.\nThe accommodation is thoughtfully laid out, providing a welcoming and light-filled interior that has been carefully maintained over the years. The rooms are generously proportioned, creating a warm and inviting atmosphere throughout. To the front, a significant feature of the property is the extensive off-street parking, with space for up to three cars, a rare and valuable asset in such a convenient location.\nTo the rear lies a sunny west-facing garden designed with ease of maintenance in mind, offering the perfect outdoor retreat for al fresco dining, entertaining guests or simply enjoying the afternoon and evening sunshine. The private garden provides a wonderful extension of the living space and is ideally suited to modern lifestyles.\nThe location is second to none, with a superb range of amenities within easy reach. Residents enjoy convenient access to local shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, schools and sporting facilities, while nearby parks and coastal walks provide excellent recreational opportunities. The property is exceptionally well served by public transport, with regular Dublin Bus routes and nearby DART services offering swift access to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas. The N11, M50 and major road networks are also easily accessible, making commuting particularly convenient.\nCombining a sought-after location, generous parking, a sunny west-facing garden and well-presented accommodation, 91 Pearse Gardens presents an excellent opportunity to acquire a wonderful home in a thriving and well-connected community."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nLiving Room - 2.35m x 3.96m\nlight brush oak wood plank flooring, recessed lighting\n\nEntrance Hall - \ncentral light, light brushed oak wood plank flooring\n\nKitchen/Dining - 3.07m x 6.01m\ntiled flooring, floor and eyelevel cabinets, electric hob and extractor fan, integrated electric double oven, washing machine, standalone fridge freezer, stainless steel sink unit, tiled splashback, Alarm, central lightDining area: light oak wood plank flooring, central light, door to rear garden\n\nLanding - \ncarpet flooring, central light, attic access\n\nBedroom 1 - 2.66m x 4.97m\nlight brush oak wood plank flooring, recessed lighting, double room to rear, built-in wardrobes\n\nBedroom 2 - 2.77m x 3.96m\ndouble room to front, built-in wardrobes, boiler, recessed lighting\n\nBathroom - 1.77m x 1.95m\ntiled flooring and part tiled walls, bath suite with electric Triton shower, WC, wash handbasin, window, recessed lighting\n\n"
      },
